passed through\nreadelf -l and the GNU_STACK is confirmed not to be executable anymore.\nThe Android one was unaffected.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298746\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318065\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-onnxruntime.sh"], "git_node": "d35bbf39a897586d2030866ddb4449bfeed4db8e", "git_parents": ["bf5fabf6243f48c787d6018f5f7cd656919cd277"], "node": "f7dcf62c0edc0c8ef47b651ed4d780cb5460af97", "parents": ["559482294434919eff476047aff448fd5a22e801"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786723112, "git_changesets": ["d35bbf39a897586d2030866ddb4449bfeed4db8e"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "275": {"changesets": [{"author": "Max Emig \u003cmozilla@emigm.ax\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060028 - Fix the caret position regression when inserting content into an empty block.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315934\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316674\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_insertHTML_caret_position_after_replaced_element.html"], "git_node": "a801a867c2d4859b7eece95cf57e2121c45155c3", "git_parents": ["d35bbf39a897586d2030866ddb4449bfeed4db8e"], "node": "f035962c2d2ca4aa4ac79a6aac027ee56b34ad65", "parents": ["f7dcf62c0edc0c8ef47b651ed4d780cb5460af97"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786723554, "git_changesets": ["a801a867c2d4859b7eece95cf57e2121c45155c3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "276": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054625 - WebRTC backport: Video capture: validate PipeWire camera frame size to prevent OOB read  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nCheck spa_chunk::size is not larger than mmap'ed buffer, which would\nlead to an out-of-bounds read when the frame is copied. Validate that\nchunk offset + size does not exceed maxsize before processing.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: 612430e8266881eaff478b0000cacc90fb71c918\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316000\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317422\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/612430e826.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "b2b70badc826d3ca5895a1890465c915dbbaed5e", "git_parents": ["a801a867c2d4859b7eece95cf57e2121c45155c3"], "node": "33db99d32a852dbd536d64c1e913a614f068a52b", "parents": ["f035962c2d2ca4aa4ac79a6aac027ee56b34ad65"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786723583, "git_changesets": ["b2b70badc826d3ca5895a1890465c915dbbaed5e"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "277": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054299 - WebRTC backport: Video capture: fix division by zero when framerate is unset  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nSPA_FORMAT_VIDEO_framerate is optional in the PipeWire format pod. When\nabsent or zero, the unguarded division in OnFormatChanged() causes\na SIGFPE crash. Initialize format structs and fallback to max_framerate\nor a default of 30 FPS.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: 67becacf3c88a16f7118766492439863406852cf\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317736\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317787\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/video_capture_pipewire.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/67becacf3c.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "43a9d5b5de9ae35fde3fcaab8d85dd8f3af3ae87", "git_parents": ["b2b70badc826d3ca5895a1890465c915dbbaed5e"], "node": "e2dd824b3c2482d6bfc3b22ccf6574f4692ee686", "parents": ["33db99d32a852dbd536d64c1e913a614f068a52b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786723653, "git_changesets": ["43a9d5b5de9ae35fde3fcaab8d85dd8f3af3ae87"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "278": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan Grulich \u003cjgrulich@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054619 - WebRTC backport: Video capture: validate SPA pod values to prevent OOB reads  a=RyanVM\n\nAdd bounds checks when reading SPA pod choice values in OnNodeParam\nand ParseFormat. Validate that the pod value size matches the expected\ntype using spa_pod_type_size() and that the number of choice items\nis sufficient before accessing the underlying arrays.\n\nThis is a simple backport of an WebRTC upstream change.\n\nUpstream commit: a0253ec15b3d3072fb35d6be29ba9224c36f9dd7\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318394\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318414\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/pipewire_session.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/a0253ec15b.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "68f48b595635c0843f793ddf0a24ac9ee6e0bb7c", "git_parents": ["43a9d5b5de9ae35fde3fcaab8d85dd8f3af3ae87"], "node": "cab811203d9ddaf79fb111451d7e96412560aa18", "parents": ["e2dd824b3c2482d6bfc3b22ccf6574f4692ee686"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786723677, "git_changesets": ["68f48b595635c0843f793ddf0a24ac9ee6e0bb7c"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "279": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Backed out changeset 68f48b595635 (bug 2054619) for Linux build bustage. a=backout\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_capture/linux/pipewire_session.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/a0253ec15b.no-op-cherry-pick-msg"], "git_node": "0316783e66e58dad2142d230655f10016a9645b8", "git_parents": ["68f48b595635c0843f793ddf0a24ac9ee6e0bb7c"], "node": "7ffae4f3f915cc12b53831af144d60c504c5653d", "parents": ["cab811203d9ddaf79fb111451d7e96412560aa18"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786726894, "gi