n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318974\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_snap.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_node.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_tree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/aa/fractional-nine-patch.png", "layout/reftests/async-scrolling/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/position-sticky/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/transform-3d/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-transforms/individual-transform/animation/individual-transform-combine.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/new-content-inline-with-offset-from-containing-block-clipped.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/responsive/toggle-animated-iframe-visibility.html.ini"], "git_node": "b3fccc955ae3245811a6bdb9c48cad8800f6b2a9", "git_parents": ["64143c6d188c7ff2e9870fb170c670efd6bed0dd"], "node": "4d8c489cb6bd526565160fdb7e1b030a1992785b", "parents": ["90d768f7620f61d0f6322c0e1ef5c16f6f72cc75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063932 - Revert \"Bug 2044211 - Refactor text runs to store glyphs with device offsets\"  a=RyanVM\n\nThis reverts commit d5009a5aac185551d484597c8d469ee2679cea7d.\n\nReverting cleanly requires reverting bug 2045926 and bug 2004666 first, which this\nseries does; the only hand-merged part left is one line in\nscene_building.rs::add_text. The restored code recovered the display-list-space\nprim origin as prim_info.rect.min - offset, with offset coming from\ncurrent_external_scroll_offset(). Bug 2044856 landed after the patch being\nreverted here, moved that normalization into the display-list builder and deleted\nthe helper, so the external scroll offset is already removed from both the glyph\npositions and the prim rect. dl_prim_origin is therefore prim_info.rect.min with\nthe - offset term dropped; keeping it would subtract the offset twice.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318975\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_text_run.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list"], "git_node": "66dd6d529909fc0a1c8e7131140d1419c02dd722", "git_parents": ["b3fccc955ae3245811a6bdb9c48cad8800f6b2a9"], "node": "4731ba4a8fc51b2ae012f6b93fa4ab5930a2984a", "parents": ["4d8c489cb6bd526565160fdb7e1b030a1992785b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787004866, "git_changesets": ["64143c6d188c7ff2e9870fb170c670efd6bed0dd", "b3fccc955ae3245811a6bdb9c48cad8800f6b2a9", "66dd6d529909fc0a1c8e7131140d1419c02dd722"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "321": {"changesets": [{"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052162 - metadata update. a=test-only\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/printing/table-in-flex-overflow-print.html.ini"], "git_node": "254997b388507e0f5a10e521db7fab7c344c3955", "git_parents": ["66dd6d529909fc0a1c8e7131140d1419c02dd722"], "node": "04a1289b1eb09fa8b4ee2f042e37670ce0bee649", "parents": ["4731ba4a8fc51b2ae012f6b93fa4ab5930a2984a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040973 - Wait for the address doorhanger to be localized before clicking its edit link, r=dimi a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315462\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "3d7b3ff5f3969a7ee112dffb347677ad86f5a95c", "git_parents": ["254997b388507e0f5a10e521db7fab7c344c3955"], "node": "5fd5ffd99f0c82c876d117f0513d54e59f433aa7", "parents": ["04a1289b1eb09fa8b4ee2f042e37670ce0bee649"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040973 - Load the address doorhanger's strings before showing it, r=dimi a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315463\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "58ba05c4a273fa9428453511b9190ae9441e52c4", "git_parents": ["3d7b3ff5f3969a7ee112dffb347677ad86f5a95c"], "node": "fb7af6a2123f77594721ad2062099bed08c832ce", "parents": ["5fd5ffd99f0c82c876d117f0513d54e59f433aa7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1697626 - Wait for the extension onRequestFinished listener to be registered before navigating in browser_ext_devtools_network.js, and re-enable the test, r=extension-reviewers,rpl a=test-only DONTBUILD\n\nRegistering the listener is asynchronous on the parent side and the test\nnavigates immediately after asking for it, so PAYLOAD_READY can be emitted and\ndropped before the listener exists. The test navigates only once, so it then\nwaits forever. Poll hasRequestFinishedListeners() before navigating.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317522\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-devtools.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_devtools_network.js"], "git_node": "2b85e141a7c03c68050083d560f427b7e5ebdf1f", "git_parents": ["58ba05c4a273fa9428453511b9190ae9441e52c4"], "node": "fb21a33d635730994ce24f18e6424e2bfd3a0396", "parents": ["fb7af6a2123f77594721ad2062099bed08c832ce"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787016523, "git_changesets": ["254997b388507e0f5a10e521db7fab7c344c3955", "3d7b3ff5f3969a7ee112dffb347677ad86f5a95c", "58ba05c4a273fa9428453511b9190ae9441e52c4", "2b85e141a7c03c68050083d560f427b7e5ebdf1f"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "322": {"changesets": [{"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061801 - Get principal from dragContent if it doesn't come from a remote process.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317134\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319141\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "widget/nsDragServiceProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "30258b437f3fcc15762d11d1736cd6a3d2e7b2e9", "git_parents": ["2b85e141a7c03c68050083d560f427b7e5ebdf1f"], "node": "574a6f0463338a87c362db793bb8b43c923846fd", "parents": ["fb21a33d635730994ce24f18e6424e2bfd3a0396"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061801 - Part 2: Remove #ifdef MOZ_THUNDERBIRD guard for drag+drop principal.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318117\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319142\n", "files": ["widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "7c986da5e4012b5f478211efaf6a926f688372fd", "git_parents": ["30258b437f3fcc15762d11d1736cd6a3d2e7b2e9"], "node": "935fefe782c805895800b4768f062d42192f7159", "parents": ["574a6f0463338a87c362db793bb8b43c923846fd"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787017095, "git_changesets": ["30258b437f3fcc15762d11d1736cd6a3d2e7b2e9", "7c986da5e4012b5f478211efaf6a926f688372fd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "323": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056118 - Step back in numeric mode if identical prefix ends with digit but only one of left or right starts with digit.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318712\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319005\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/non262/Intl/Collator/numeric.js", "third_party/rust/icu_collator/src/comparison.rs"], "git_node": "f5daf9e001c64f75ab63cd9b09cd35adc7a69673", "git_parents": ["7c986da5e4012b5f478211efaf6a926f688372fd"], "node": "069f5c911cf2f727dc9efd3152a27c8cb96ecdf1", "parents": ["935fefe782c805895800b4768f062d42192f7159"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787017188, "git_changesets": ["f5daf9e001c64f75ab63cd9b09cd35adc7a69673"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "324": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059047 - Reset looked_ahead when resetting drain_from_upcoming.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nUpstream issue: https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x/issues/8296\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318684\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319008\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/non262/Intl/Collator/contraction.js", "third_party/rust/icu_collator/src/elements.rs"], "git_node": "29aaf08baae0cbff6519c8193d894a8cf9103881", "git_parents": ["f5daf9e001c64f75ab63cd9b09cd35adc7a69673"], "node": "a69b3f6de888bf7054bdda76f56504c1567f81ab", "parents": ["069f5c911cf2f727dc9efd3152a27c8cb96ecdf1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787017213, "git_changesets": ["29aaf08baae0cbff6519c8193d894a8cf9103881"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "325": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058661 - Clear the drag source window's GdkDragContext pointer synchronously. r=stransky a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\ngtk_drag_begin_with_coordinates() returns a borrowed context: GtkDragSourceInfo\nholds the only reference, and gtk_drag_source_info_destroy() drops it as soon as\nthe drag-end handler returns. nsWindow::mSourceDragContext was cleared only from\nan async runnable (EndDragSessionMainThread -\u003e EndDragSessionImpl), so between\nGTK's unref and that runnable the pointer dangled, and nsWindow::OnUnmap() calls\ngtk_drag_cancel() on it. Content can land an unmap in that window with a\nwindow.close() task queued before the drag ended.\n\nEndDragSessionImpl keeps its own clear for drags torn down without a drag-end.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315509\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319278\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "2987a6b5a4adaae8ad52288f2d7d3bb103092200", "git_parents": ["29aaf08baae0cbff6519c8193d894a8cf9103881"], "node": "d474cc4f4937d1496c2be67579b1b422a95f7f28", "parents": ["a69b3f6de888bf7054bdda76f56504c1567f81ab"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787017238, "git_changesets": ["2987a6b5a4adaae8ad52288f2d7d3bb103092200"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "326": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2015253 - Only return a container frame top level docs during print preview.  a=RyanVM\n\nThis matches the pre-regression logic, and fixes the coordinate system\nof the slicing fragmentation fallback.\n\nUnfortunately testing this is kind of a PITA, because the obvious way to\ndo it would be WPT print reftests, but that requires e10s. Regular\nreftests don't have any print stuff that would reliably test the\nfragmentation fallback I think?\n\nI can try to come up with something tho...\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318966\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D319052\n", "files": ["layout/printing/nsPrintJob.cpp"], "git_node": "0502ef835c3af552536b9379596e8bcc0e8376d3", "git_parents": ["2987a6b5a4adaae8ad52288f2d7d3bb103092200"], "node": "61aa1cbf50dcc935f7dd43c77d2e46a51696bccd", "parents": ["d474cc4f4937d1496c2be67579b1b422a95f7f28"], "tags": []}], "date": 1787017260, "git_changesets": ["0502ef835c3af552536b9379596e8bcc0e8376d3"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "327": {"c